<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch13-chapter-ht-compare-proportions" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Comparing Groups - Categorical Response</title>
  
  <introduction>
    <p>This chapter begins with a lesson on summarizing data when you have two categorical variables. 
      Then students will extend what they have learned in the previous chapter to perform randomization tests for comparing two or more
      population proportions. Students will continue learning about study design and confounding variables. 
    </p>
  </introduction>


